Z||000000||FieroLisa||05-09-2001||04:57 PM||||Well It's about that time to look into some new sail panels for the GT. I've found two different ones, both around $200, but haven't heard much about either of them. Have any of you guys bought them (links below)  I'm most worried about them fitting correctly, rather than opinion on how they look.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fieroheaven.com/GTQuarterWindows.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroheaven.com/GTQuarterWindows.htm</A> <P>and on the one below you're going to have to scroll through some pics to get to the sail panel one. <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/kento/F355.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/kento/F355.html</A> <P><BR>Also if anyone knows of any other good companies that make nice sail panels, please give me the link!<P>Thanks!<BR><P>------------------<BR>Lisa<BR>86 violet pearl 4 speed GT: 17 in. rims, lowered, cold-air intake<BR>AOL IM: FieroLisa<P><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/" TARGET=_blank>FieroLisa's Website</A><P><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/ncfieros/" TARGET=_blank>Tarheels Fieros Website</A>||||reg||1
Z||000001||rogergarrison||05-09-2001||05:07 PM||||make sure you find the instructions to replace them too, lisa, cause I know your gonna ask me to show you - and Ive never messed with them before.||||reg||1
Z||000002||stimpy||05-09-2001||05:15 PM||||Definately go with Doug Kinney's sails. <A HREF="http://geocities.com/fierowarehouse/" TARGET=_blank>http://geocities.com/fierowarehouse/</A> <P>I have a set on mine and I was very happy with the prompt delivery and the excellent fit. I've never heard of the second link, but I have heard some extremely negative feedback on Fiero Heaven.<P>When you install them, apply the tape to the sail panel then put it on to the car. Otherwise the tape maybe visible. Kinda tacky.   <p>[This message has been edited by stimpy (edited 05-09-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||skitime||05-09-2001||06:37 PM||||GM makes a nice set of panels and they fit perfect and look as good as the orginals. They are not as cheap but the real things rarely are.  Just got two this week at <A HREF="http://www.gmparsdirect.com" TARGET=_blank>www.gmparsdirect.com</A>   The first set lasted 13 years how long are brand X going to last?<P>Parts number 20701106 & 20701107 at 295.37 including shipping.<BR>  <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||stsmithgt||05-09-2001||06:59 PM||||I bought some through the dealership.  I was worried that the plexiglass would yellow and I heard the ones from the dealer are lexan.  The only thing is to keep harsh cleansers away from them like alcohol based cleaners.  For instance, if you spray lexan with carb cleaner, it will change it's molicular structure from a strong flexible material to a brittle material that shatters.  Hmmm, wonder why so many cars have crackled panels?  I used a RAIN-X cleaning product on my old ones and I won't touch my new ones with that stuff.  WELL THAT'S WHAT I'VE HEARD ANYWAY.  I've tried looking up info. on the web to find out how to take care of it since it's used in so many different applications, but haven't found what I'm looking for yet.  <P>Whoops, long winded.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> LATER!||||reg||1
Z||000005||RobertVol||05-09-2001||07:10 PM||||Lisa,<P>I agree with Stimpy on this. <P>I have a pair of Doug Kinney's. Sure you can go with Stock if you can get them. But unless you have to go with stock I would use Doug's. They look great. I have met Doug and had dealings with him.By the way he was at Daytona. He is great guy to do business with. And if something is wrong he will make it right.  I have a pic of his windows on my car here some where. When I can I will post it. <P>Also they will not get the small cracking you get with the stock ones. PLus they are cheaper <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> which always helps <BR>------------------<BR>Robert<BR>88GT 56k T TOP  <BR>North Florida Fiero Club<P>CLICK BELOW AND SEE OUR SITE !!! <A HREF="http://fullspeed.to/NorthFLFieros" TARGET=_blank>http://fullspeed.to/NorthFLFieros</A><BR>   <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=819451&a=5959473&p=36934984&Sequence=1">  <p>[This message has been edited by RobertVol (edited 05-09-2001).]||||reg||1
