Z||000010||stsmithgt||05-10-2001||03:34 PM||||Those do look nice.  Acrylic is tough stuff too.  I paid 100.00 more to get the original ones.  Why?  The fear of receiving them damaged or lost in the mail and having to deal with the shipping company and re-ordering more to possibly go through that again.  I guess I'm old school still.  The dealership was free shipping and on my way home from work so it was real convenient.  The left one came in 3 days, but the right one took almost a month.  Oh well, it took me longer than that to get around to putting them on. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000011||AusFiero||05-10-2001||07:09 PM||||God I wished I lived in America when it comes time to buy Fiero parts. I had to pay $1050 (about $550 US) for a pair of GT sail panel windows. But we have hefty duties from our government cause they think anyone who owns an American car must have lots of money to give them.<P>Ok had my whinge now  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>Resume.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero.gif"> <BR>When I was young I spent 80% of my money on Women, Gambling and Alcohol. I guess I wasted the rest.||||reg||8
Z||000012||wkayl||05-10-2001||09:50 PM||||I just backed my car out of the garage this evening to get it ready for a show this weekend.  Everything was fine on Sunday when I drove it, but now I have a 2in. crack on the drivers side quarter window.  I have "0" deductable on glass and they replaced my pass side last year ($300+).  I told them it was a stress crack.  I'll try this one and see if they fix it. <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/twocars.jpg"> ||||reg||1
